        "Seventeen companies that turn steel, iron, aluminium and copper alloys into the parts that make an engine, gearbox, wheel or brake work: pistons and rings, crankshafts and axle beams, bearing rings and engine bearings, gears, gaskets, fasteners, camshafts, tyre bead wire and aluminium die-castings. This is one of five groups on the Auto Related page; the others cover EV, electronics and electrical content, batteries and brand-led replacement, truck, tractor, off-highway and rail systems, and vehicle systems and assemblies for two-wheeler and car makers. Six make **engine and powertrain parts**: **Shriram Pistons** (renamed SPR Auto Technologies), **Craftsman Automation**, **Talbros**, **Menon Bearings**, **RACL Geartech** and **Precision Camshafts**. Four make **forgings, bearing rings and steel wire**: **CIE Automotive**, **Ramkrishna Forgings**, **Rolex Rings** and **Rajratan Global Wire**. Seven make **castings, fasteners and precision components**: **ASK Automotive**, **Alicon**, **Rico Auto**, **Poojaa Precision**, **OBSC Perfection**, **Sundram Fasteners** and **Sterling Tools**. This edition was built from both earnings calls for every company that holds them, the Q1 FY27 presentations, the FY26 annual reports (auditor's reports, related parties, contingent liabilities), rating reports from CRISIL, ICRA and CARE, and sector work from ACMA, Crisil Ratings, ICRA, CareEdge and Elara Capital. The headline: Q1 FY27 revenue looked superb, but much of it was the GST-cut lift in vehicle volumes, aluminium prices passed on to customers, and acquisitions; margins fell almost everywhere, and ICRA expects truck volumes to fall in H2 FY27. The annual reports turned up a ₹220cr inventory overstatement and ₹525cr of joint-venture loan support at Ramkrishna Forgings, a government investigation at Precision Camshafts that its annual report does not mention, a drafting note left in Poojaa's published report, promoter-family selling at Menon and Craftsman, and plant bought from a promoter company at Alicon. Every chart uses filed results.",
